## 6️⃣ Going further

| Want to… | How to extend |
|----------|----------------|
| **Use a custom colour palette** (e.g. Viridis, Plasma) | Replace the hex strings in `colorRamp` with the palette values. You can generate a ramp with a small script or use an online tool like <https://github.com/d3/d3-scale-chromatic>. |
| **Show a legend** | Create a simple HTML `<div>` that mirrors the stops you used (`<svg>` rectangles + labels). |
| **Animate the colour on hover** | Use `setFeatureState` + a `circle-color` expression that checks `['feature-state', 'hover']`. Remember to `promoteId`. |
| **Load from a vector-tile server** | Change the source to `{type:'vector', url:'https://example.com/tiles.json'}` and add `source-layer: 'your_layer_name'` to the layer definition. The same `circle-color` expression works unchanged. |
| **Performance-tune** | If you have thousands of points, consider clustering (`cluster: true`) and style the clusters separately. |

