## 4️⃣  Bonus: Adding a legend (optional)

If you want a tiny legend that shows the colour ramp:

```html
<div id="legend" style="background:white;padding:6px;font:12px sans-serif;">
  <strong>Population</strong><br>
  <svg width="120" height="12">
    <defs>
      <linearGradient id="popGrad" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="0%">
        <stop offset="0%"   stop-color="#e0f3ff"/>
        <stop offset="20%"  stop-color="#c6e2ff"/>
        <stop offset="40%"  stop-color="#8abed8"/>
        <stop offset="60%"  stop-color="#5699c1"/>
        <stop offset="80%"  stop-color="#2c6ea5"/>
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#004080"/>
      </linearGradient>
    </defs>
    <rect width="120" height="12" fill="url(#popGrad)"/>
  </svg>
  <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;">
    <span>0</span><span>1 M+</span>
  </div>
</div>
```

Place the `<div id="legend">…</div>` anywhere on the page (e.g., top-right corner) and you have a visual cue that “darker = more people”.

